## #16 — ACF setup, Global Fields, `getGlobalSettings()` pattern

### Global Fields (Global Settings page)

| Field | Name | Type | Return Value | Frontend |
|-------|------|------|--------------|----------|
| Logo Image | `logo_image` | Image | — | Intro ✅ |
| Bio Image | `bio_image` | Image | — | Not yet wired |
| Logo Video | `logo_video` | File | **File URL** | Intro ✅ |

- **Show in REST API** must be **ON** for every field group.
- ACF Gallery/Repeater = Pro only; use media tags for galleries on free tier.

### `getGlobalSettings()` pattern

```typescript
export async function getGlobalSettings(): Promise<WPGlobalSettings> {
  const url = `${WP_API_URL}/pages?slug=global-settings&acf_format=standard`;
  const res = await fetch(url, { cache: 'no-store' });
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Failed to fetch global settings: ${res.status}`);
  const pages = await res.json();
  if (!pages.length) throw new Error('Global Settings page not found');
  return pages[0].acf as unknown as WPGlobalSettings;
}
```

### `WPGlobalSettings` interface

```typescript
export interface WPGlobalSettings {
  logo_image?: WPImage | null;
  bio_image?: WPImage | null;
  logo_video?: ACFMediaFile | string | null | false;
}
```

### Video resolution chain (`lib/wordpress.ts`)

- `resolveIntroVideo(logoVideo)` — tries ACF first, falls back to `INTRO_VIDEO_URL` env var
- `resolveLogoVideoField(logoVideo)` — extracts `{ url, type }` from object or plain string
- `acfFileFieldUrl(value)` — handles `false`, `null`, string, or object shapes
- `videoSourceTypeFromUrl(url)` — infers `video/mp4`, `video/webm`, `video/ogg` from extension

Since ACF field is set to **File URL**, WordPress returns a plain string; `acfFileFieldUrl` handles this path.

